{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Remember</b> — he seeks His mercies and kindnesses, that He not requite him for his former deeds, which hindered him until now from understanding the ways of HaShem in truth; therefore after it: 'my sins and my transgressions' — the transgression is that the transgressor goes out from under authority, and it is witness to every matter of transgression." "And by reason of 'like Your kindness' — because You are the source of kindness and the wellspring of good, therefore after it: 'good,' with an open bet in 'in the way,' for it is the way of HaShem as he began: 'Your ways, YHWH, make known to me.' And behold, He will guide the sinners as to which is the straight way, and the humble He will lead in His way and accustom them, until it becomes for them a statute and a judgment."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is syntactically compressed and the clause relations are not fully articulated; translated hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:33.423868638Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}